.TH DOCKSTAR 1 "July 2026" "Dockstar" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dockstar \- display docking automation for KDE Plasma Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dockstar
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Dockstar detects approved external displays, applies a Plasma display layout,
and coordinates optional audio, network, power, lock, and suspend actions.
The daemon exposes a versioned session D-Bus API used by the CLI, tray, and
settings window.
.PP
Version 1 supports Linux amd64 running KDE Plasma 6 on Wayland with systemd
257 or newer. A fresh configuration uses an empty display allowlist and does
not change privileged hardware wake state.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B daemon
Run the foreground daemon. Normally started by the systemd user service.
.TP
.B status
Print complete daemon state as JSON.
.TP
.B devices
Print the normalized output array as JSON.
.TP
.BI allow " DEVICE_ID"
Approve a display for allowlist detection, creating a default rule if needed.
.TP
.BI deny " DEVICE_ID"
Deny a display without deleting its saved rule.
.TP
.BI trust " all|allowlist|off"
Set the external display detection policy.
.TP
.BI mode " extend|mirror|external-only|internal-only"
Save the default layout and immediately force evaluation.
.TP
.B apply
Force display evaluation and rerun active dock actions after a successful
layout transaction.
.TP
.B suspend
Temporarily release Dockstar sleep protection and request one intentional
suspend through systemd-logind. Protection is restored after resume.
.TP
.B diagnose
Print state, environment, backend, config path, and wake diagnostics as JSON.
.TP
.BI wake " status|enable|disable|restore"
Inspect or configure hardware wake sources. Changes require an installed
system helper and Polkit authentication. Restore returns sources to their
first-recorded baseline.
.TP
.BI startup " status|enable|sync|disable"
Inspect or configure approved-device sleep protection before graphical login.
Enable requires administrator authentication and snapshots explicitly approved
EDID displays into a root-owned system policy. Sync updates that policy after
approval changes, including the final revocation, which disables protection.
The system service hands over when session protection is ready or after a
fixed 15-second login timeout; it does not configure layouts or automatic login.
.TP
.B config show
Load, validate, and print the active configuration.
.TP
.BI config " validate [PATH]"
Validate a JSON configuration file, or the active file when no path is given.
.TP
.BI completion " bash|zsh|fish"
Print basic shell completion definitions.
.TP
.B version
Print version, commit, and build date.
.SH LAYOUTS
.TP
.B extend
Enable the internal panel and approved externals with an external primary.
.TP
.B mirror
Replicate the selected external primary to the internal panel using the best
common mode under the configured refresh cap.
.TP
.B external-only
Enable approved external displays and disable the internal panel.
.TP
.B internal-only
Disable external displays and enable the internal panel.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DOCKSTAR_CONFIG
Override the complete configuration path.
.TP
.B DOCKSTAR_DEBUG
Set to 1 for daemon debug logging.
.TP
.B DOCKSTAR_WAKE_HELPER
Override the wake helper path, primarily for controlled tests.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for user configuration when DOCKSTAR_CONFIG is unset.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Base directory for the latest runtime state snapshot.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dockstar/config.json
Persistent schema-versioned user configuration.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/dockstar/state.json
Latest runtime status snapshot.
.TP
.I /etc/dockstar/wake.json
Root-owned desired hardware wake policy.
.TP
.I /var/lib/dockstar/wake-baseline.json
First-recorded hardware wake states used by restore.
.TP
.I /var/lib/dockstar/startup.json
Root-owned pre-login protection policy and explicitly approved EDID identities.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. Invalid arguments, unavailable D-Bus services,
configuration errors, rejected display transactions, failed commands, or wake
helper failures return nonzero.
.SH SLEEP PROTECTION
When Keep computer awake while docked is enabled, Dockstar holds a strict
systemd-logind sleep inhibitor for an approved dock. Ordinary Plasma Sleep may
therefore be blocked. Use
.B dockstar suspend
or the equivalent settings or tray action to release protection for one
intentional suspend cycle. Dockstar does not rewrite Plasma power settings or
logind configuration.
.SH SECURITY
The wake helper, startup helper, and hardened startup guard run with
administrator privileges. The session daemon, ordinary CLI commands, tray,
and settings window run as the desktop user.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR systemd-sleep (8),
.BR kscreen-doctor (1),
.BR busctl (1),
.BR pkexec (1)
.PP
Full documentation is available at
https://github.com/redundercover/dockstar/tree/main/docs.
